# Commands run by the launchd job com.redwood.demo (RC_JOBS=rc.jobs.metalcompute).
#
# How many Metal compute kernels of the system's own libraries this driver can actually run.
#
# The list is every kernel of the corpus that binds nothing but buffers -- the driver has no
# textures yet, and the compiler library refuses a shader that wants one by name rather than
# binding nothing -- MINUS the ones tools/air/kstruct.py measured as unable to terminate on a
# harness's input: a loop that leaves only on a value the buffers do not contain does not
# leave, and docs/air.md section 5 is about what one hung dispatch does to everything after it
# (gpuWait latches, every later wait returns false at once, and the next boot panics).
#
# So: 16 kernels bind only buffers, 7 of those cannot end, 9 are here. Each runs in its own
# process, so that one crash costs one kernel rather than the rest of the list.
/redwood/bin/metal_drv_test /System/Library/CoreImage/PortraitFilters.cifilter/default.metallib MetalFaceMask_InitMinMax
/redwood/bin/metal_drv_test /System/Library/CoreImage/PortraitFilters.cifilter/default.metallib MetalFaceMask_CalcCubeInputScaling
/redwood/bin/metal_drv_test /System/Library/CoreImage/PortraitFilters.cifilter/default.metallib MetalFaceMask_InitSpanTable
/redwood/bin/metal_drv_test /System/Library/CoreImage/PortraitFilters.cifilter/default.metallib MetalFaceMask_PropogateAssociations
/redwood/bin/metal_drv_test /System/Library/CoreImage/PortraitFilters.cifilter/default.metallib fbs_bistochastize_init
/redwood/bin/metal_drv_test /System/Library/CoreImage/PortraitFilters.cifilter/default.metallib fbs_pcg_iter2
/redwood/bin/metal_drv_test /System/Library/CoreImage/PortraitFilters.cifilter/default.metallib fbs_pcg_iter3
/redwood/bin/metal_drv_test /System/Library/CoreImage/PortraitFilters.cifilter/default.metallib image_calcminmax0
/redwood/bin/metal_drv_test /System/Library/CoreImage/PortraitFilters.cifilter/default.metallib image_calcminmax2
#
# And one triangle, with one of Apple's own fragment shaders: clearFragment20 writes render
# target 2 and is one of the 255 air_run has drawn and compared pixel by pixel, so there is
# something to compare the Adreno's answer against. The pipeline is asked for with no vertex
# function, which is the compiler library's cue to generate a pass-through stage over the
# whole attachment -- the same road air_run itself draws by.
/redwood/bin/metal_drv_test --draw /System/Library/Extensions/AppleMetalGLRenderer.bundle/default.metallib
